s  accommodation living expenses and even  transportation past charges  the third benefit we have on our list is  excellent infrastructure and facilities  that germany offers  higher education in germany consists of  three different types of institutions  universities universities of applied  sciences technical arts film and music  colleges  and most of those universities date from  the middle ages bearing the significant  tradition of qualitative education and  prominent names in various academic  disciplines  according to the official statistics of  2018 there are 429 recognized  universities in germany out of which 106  are among the list of globally ranked  universities  some of them have been ranked among the  world's best universities consistently  five of highest ranking universities in  germany are technical universities of  munich  dude with max milan university munich  heddelberg university  kashule institute of technology and  humboldt university berlin  germany as a whole place great value on  education and this is reflected in the  high quality teaching seen in country  international students can experience  the excellent quality of the education  on offer through english language driven  courses  degree courses are constantly updated to  meet the changing business world  students are given the opportunity to  utilize cutting-edge technology and the  latest research to ensure they are ready  to enter the world of work after  graduation  the fourth benefit of studying in  germany is that you are allowed to work  for part-time opportunities as per  german law international students with  student visa are allowed to work for 120  full days or 240 half days during the  year  when the semester is on you can work for  20 hours a week  whereas during vacations you can work  full time you will not require any type  of approval for this you can  automatically work for 20 hours a week  the moment you have a national visa for  a student  the part-time job opportunities revolve  around the store and restaurant shifts  language tutoring field interviewing or  a call center industry however you will  be required to master the german  language to get these interactive jobs  let's look at the remuneration  the minimum wage in germany is 9 euros  per hour but you get up to 15 to 18  euros per hour if you work as a call  center employee or operations assistant  looking at the 20 hours a week you could  earn up to 800 euros a month which would  sufficiently take care of your living  cost  also you could keep in mind that if you  earn more than 450 euros a month you'll  have to pay taxes and social security  contributions  and since you'll be working as a student  these charges will pan out to be quite  minimal  the fifth benefit on our list is better  job prospects  as you might know germany is the fourth  largest economy in the world after the  united states china and japan  also it is the largest economy in the  eastern european continent  because of that there are plenty of jobs  available for international students  with technical expertise  however to get the jobs you are required  to have german language proficiency  be one of language proficiency is the  bare minimum before you can look out for  any permanent job  let's talk about sectors that produce  maximum job opportunities in germany  the first one is information technology  as you know the world is gravitating  towards completely virtualization since  covet pandemic the requirements for it  experts in germany has increased  exponentially  according to the survey there are around  124 000 open jobs for id professionals  in germany  that's why it is at the top of our list  the next sector that produces more jobs  in germany is engineering  particularly mechanical engineering and  automobile engineering are the  trailblazers that produce a pool of job  opportunities you can also find abundant  jobs related to the electronics robotics  and chemical engineering sectors the  renewable power sector is another  growing industry that aims to develop  sustainable growth in germany and  another sector that has huge potential  is medical science  germany has always been a big  contributor to the global medical sector  hence  it is quite beneficial to explore this  field  the local companies that have  professionals for various sectors  are douche bank robert bosch  aliens finances siemens bmw wolfsbacon  autos hugo boss and adidas sportswear  and shoes  the top multinational companies that  operate and hire professionals in  germany are amazon google mckenzie and  company kpmg posh and mercedes-benz all  these companies have a significant  presence in germany and employ a large  number of professionals  however german universities have their  own career centers since these  universities are of global accreditation  and have strong ties with all local and  multinational companies and can help you  set your career on the track of growth  the next benefit of studying in germany  is the opportunity to settle down  typically after you finish your  university studies your student visa  will expire almost immediately even if  the visa was initially granted for  period longer than the period of your  degree after this expiration you'll be  eligible to apply for an 18-month work  visa during this period of 18 months  you'll have to search for permanent job  also you'll lose out on student benefits  such as subsidized health insurance and  free travel card  now as soon as you get a permanent job  you'll be eligible for part-time german  residence permit or eu blue card the  difference between these permits is  really as the name suggests the german  residence permit is restricted for the  jobs within germany whereas the eu blue  card allows you to move around between  the countries of eastern europe  however it is said that the german  residence card is prepared for better  long-term prospects within germany so  make sure you contemplate the pros and  cons of these two permits before  selecting one  in the next phase you will be eligible  for permanent german residence or a  permanent eu blue card depending on your  preference however you'll have to work  for a tenure of four years in germany to  apply for permanent residency  that's all we have about the benefits of  studying in germany however if you don't  have the required capital support to do  so we recommend you to look out for  global psw programs available online  these programs can help you accelerate  your career in the global market with  the least financial requirements  simplylearn offers one such management  program in collaboration with iu germany  you can now get access to the best that  iu has to offer study on campus build an  international management career and get  an opportunity to work in germany with  this master of business administration  mba program with iu germany and london  south bank university lsba you can  become a global management industry  leader  furthermore after successful completion  of this course you will be able to  launch a career in german corporations  with an 18 month long post study work  visa  here are a few highest paying  opportunities that you can get in  germany after finishing this accredited  mba program  the average base salary for finance  professionals in germany range around  almost 89 000 euros which pan out to be  75 lakh rupees in india  the base salary for marketing  professionals is almost 65  600 euros having an equivalence of  almost 54 lakh indian rupees  the next mba specialization that is  business analytics also has fruitful  salaries starting from 60 000 euros  the fourth one is the operations and  logistic salaries starting from a base  pay of 72 000 euros  and finally human resources  professionals in germany can earn up to  50 000 euros having equivalence around  42 lakh indian rupees  all these numbers mentioned above are  quite fruitful compared to the salaries  in other developing countries so  thinking about this program is worth a  while that's all we have for today  thank you for watching this video and  stay tuned for more from simply learn  hi there if you like this video  subscribe to the simply learn youtube  channel and click here to watch similar  videos to nerd up and get certified  click here  you
 

